Eqwalize all opted-in modules in specified buck target

Usage: elp eqwalize-target [OPTIONS] <TARGET>

Arguments:
  <TARGET>  target, like //erl/chatd/...

Options:
      --project <PROJECT>  Path to directory with project, or to a JSON file [default: .]
      --format <FORMAT>    Customize the output format (defaults to human-readable) [possible
                           values: json]
      --connect            Use the persistent daemon for fast turnaround (default; auto-starts if
                           needed). Pass --no-connect to disable
      --no-connect         Disable the persistent daemon and run standalone (no cross-run caching)
      --bail-on-error      Exit with a non-zero status code if any errors are found
  -h, --help               Print help

Global options:
      --log-file <LOG_FILE>  
      --erl <ERL>            
      --escript <ESCRIPT>    
      --no-log-buffering     
      --no-buck-generated    Deprecated (no-op): buck project loading always builds generated code
      --buck-quick-start     Deprecated (no-op): buck project loading always builds generated code
      --color <WHEN>         Use color in output [default: always] [possible values: always, never,
                             auto]
